## What is this?

Claude Code is Anthropic's official agentic coding CLI — it reads your codebase, writes and edits files, runs commands, and reasons through complex tasks. Normally it requires an Anthropic subscription or API credits.

This guide shows you how to point Claude Code at **OpenRouter** instead, which provides access to powerful open-source models (Llama, DeepSeek, Qwen, Nemotron, and more) **completely free of charge**.

---

## Prerequisites

- A computer running **Linux, macOS, or Windows (WSL)**
- **Node.js v18+** installed ([download here](https://nodejs.org))
- A terminal / command line

Check your Node version:
```bash
node --version
# Should output v18.x.x or higher
```

---

## Step 1 — Install Claude Code

```bash
npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
```

Verify the installation:
```bash
claude --version
```

You should see output like `Claude Code v2.x.x`.

> **Note:** If you get a permissions error on Linux/macOS, try:
> ```bash
> sudo npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
> ```
> Or configure npm to use a user-level prefix to avoid needing sudo.

