## Step 2 — Get a Free OpenRouter API Key

1. Go to [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai) and sign up (free, no credit card required)
2. Navigate to **Keys** in your account dashboard
3. Click **Create Key**
4. Copy the key — it starts with `sk-or-v1-...`

Keep this key safe. You'll use it in the next step.

---

## Step 3 — Configure Claude Code

Claude Code reads its configuration from `~/.claude/settings.json`. Create or edit this file:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.claude
nano ~/.claude/settings.json
```

Paste the following (replace `YOUR_OPENROUTER_KEY` with your actual key):

```json
{
  "env": {
    "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL": "https://openrouter.ai/api",
    "ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN": "YOUR_OPENROUTER_KEY",
    "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "",
    "ANTHROPIC_MODEL": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free"
  },
  "theme": "dark"
}
```

Save and exit (`Ctrl+O`, `Enter`, `Ctrl+X` in nano).

### Why these settings?

| Setting | Why it's needed |
|---|---|
| `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | Points Claude Code to OpenRouter instead of Anthropic |
| `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | Your OpenRouter key (Claude Code reads auth from this var) |
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Set to empty string to prevent fallback to Anthropic servers |
| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` | The free model to use (see full list below) |

> ⚠️ **Important:** Use `https://openrouter.ai/api` — NOT `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`. The `/v1` suffix causes empty response errors.

