## Tips to Stretch Your Free Tokens

1. **Start sessions fresh** — run `/clear` in Claude Code to reset conversation context before a new task

2. **Be specific with prompts** — instead of:
   > "fix my authentication system"
   
   say:
   > "fix the JWT validation bug in `src/auth/middleware.js` line 45"

3. **Use `/compact`** — this compresses the conversation history in Claude Code, saving tokens while keeping context

4. **Work on small scopes** — point Claude at specific files, not your entire repo

5. **Avoid running Claude from your home directory** — launch it from inside your project folder so it doesn't scan unrelated files

6. **Rotate models** — keep 2–3 model IDs handy so you can swap when one hits its daily limit

