## Troubleshooting

### `API returned an empty or malformed response (HTTP 200)`

**Cause:** Wrong base URL — you likely have `/v1` appended.

**Fix:** Make sure your `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` is exactly:
```
https://openrouter.ai/api
```
Not `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`.

---

### `400 — is not a valid model ID`

**Cause:** The model ID is wrong or the model was renamed/removed.

**Fix:**
1. Check the exact current model IDs at [openrouter.ai/collections/free-models](https://openrouter.ai/collections/free-models)
2. Also check if Claude Code is prepending `openrouter/` to your model name (a known bug). If so, use only `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` in the `env` block and remove the top-level `"model"` key from your settings.

---

### `Retrying in 35s · attempt X/10`

**Cause:** Rate limit hit on the free tier.

**Fix:**
- Wait a few minutes and try again
- Switch to a different free model
- Use `/clear` to shorten your context before retrying

---

### `There's an issue with the selected model — it may not exist or you may not have access`

**Cause:** The model has been taken offline or your account doesn't have access.

**Fix:** Switch to a different model from the [free models list](#free-models-you-can-use). `meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free` is the most consistently available.

---

### Claude Code shows the wrong model name in the UI

**Cause:** A project-level settings file is overriding your global config.

**Fix:** Check for project-level configs:
```bash
find ~ -name "settings.json" -path "*/.claude/*" 2>/dev/null
```
Remove or update any project-level files that have a conflicting `model` value.

---

### Still not working after all fixes?

Run this diagnostic to see exactly what config Claude Code is reading:

```bash
cat ~/.claude/settings.json
exec bash
claude --version
```

If issues persist, check OpenRouter's status at [openrouter.ai](https://openrouter.ai) — free model availability can change.

