## FAQ

**Q: Is this against Anthropic's terms of service?**  
A: Claude Code supports custom base URLs by design — this is an officially supported configuration. You are simply routing requests through OpenRouter instead of Anthropic's API.

**Q: Do free models reset daily?**  
A: Most free model limits reset every 24 hours. Some providers top up their sponsored token budgets periodically. If a model runs dry, switch to another.

**Q: Can I use this for production work?**  
A: Free tier models are fine for personal projects and development. For production or team use, consider adding OpenRouter credits ($5–10 goes a long way) for higher limits and guaranteed availability.

**Q: Why not just use `openrouter/auto`?**  
A: `openrouter/auto` rotates between available free models automatically, but you lose control over which model is used. For consistent behavior, specifying a model is better.

**Q: The model is slow — is that normal?**  
A: Free tier models are shared resources and can be slower during peak hours. Try a different model or work during off-peak times.

**Q: How do I update Claude Code?**  
A: Run `npm update -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code` to get the latest version.

